+++ b/LOGBOOK.md
@@ -5,6 +5,14 @@
 
 ## 2026-08-30
 
+### 0310 — Menu-bar update settings and deterministic scheduling (TASK-260717-rk4mi7)
+
+- HOST UX: `ReluxProxyMac` now runs as an `LSUIElement` SwiftUI `MenuBarExtra` with localized automatic-check, Check for Updates, and metadata-gated stable/pre-release controls. The host has no window-opening or application-activation path; scheduled findings stay in menu presentation, while only a user-initiated check may ask Sparkle to present in focus.
+- PERSISTENCE / SCHEDULING: UserDefaults stores only the automatic-check Boolean and channel enum. A host-only adapter applies effective values to the retained Sparkle controller, and an injected idempotent scheduler reconciles Sparkle's own cycle rather than adding a competing timer. Disabled checks remain cancelled across reconstruction.
+- PRESENTATION / SECURITY: Updater events map to idle, checking, up-to-date, available, downloading, ready-to-relaunch, and failed states backed by English String Catalog copy. Failure handling discards the source error, and tests prove that URL, path, signature, key, and token material cannot reach the fixed failure message.
+- NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: A temporary production mutation weakened `ReluxProxyUpdaterConfiguration.feedPolicy(in:)` so traversal-shaped channel metadata was admitted. The named malformed-metadata test then failed with xcodebuild exit 65; restoring the bounded `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` allowlist returned the full focused suite to green. Evidence is in `channel-gate-mutant-02.log`.
+- VALIDATION BOUNDARY: Focused Swift Testing uses injected updater/scheduler seams and a real no-start Sparkle controller; the hosted test process does not start an update check, install an update, activate the provider/system extension, or enable VPN. Unsigned host build and formatting gates are recorded under `.temp/TASK-260717-rk4mi7/`.
+
 ### 0243 — Sparkle host integration (TASK-260717-xempiv)
 
 - INTEGRATION: `ReluxProxyMac` now owns exact Sparkle 2.9.4 through the remote SPM product, a pinned resolved commit, signed-feed metadata, and one retained `SPUStandardUpdaterController`; no updater dependency entered the system extension, shared core, harness, or iOS targets.
